  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1207 PM CDT Wed Sep 2 2026\n\nAn upper level ridge will remain centered over the southeastern US \non Friday bringing additional chances for isolated storms on Friday \nafternoon and evening. Deep upper level troughing over the western \nCONUS will keep the surface pressure trough anchored near the \nTexas/New Mexico state line on Friday. Temperatures in the upper 90s \nto near 100 on the caprock on Friday will again bring high based \nconvection but with low chances of severe storms. There will be no \nrelief to the heat this weekend through at least early next week. \nThe upper level ridge currently positioned over the southeastern US \nwill shift westward with the center of the ridge nearly overhead \nduring this time period. This will likely keep convection to the \nwest of the area in New Mexico with little to no chances across West \nTexas.",
